# Editor and tool state — local to a machine, never part of the site.
.obsidian/
.claude/

# FreeFileSync writes one HTML session log per mirror run. Diagnostics, not
# history — the dated one-liner in logs/mirror_log.md is the record.
logs/mirror-ffs/

# Bill and Cowork work on alphas here while a Claude Code session is running in
# the repo. Untracked on purpose: it keeps in-progress design out of the history
# and out of any `git add -A`, so the two can work without colliding.
prep/

# BUILD writes this when a run starts and removes it when the run ends, cleanly or
# with a logged error. It survives only a run that died unannounced — a session that
# ran out of context mid-stage-4 — which is the one state RENDER Step 0 refuses to
# render, because a half-moved build typesets perfectly and passes every check.
# Untracked on purpose: it is a fact about this machine right now, not history, and
# a tracked one would land in every commit a build makes.
logs/.build-in-progress

# Staging is created outside the repo, but belt and braces.
.pull-staging/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.workroot/

# `build-finance-page.py` writes a per-place {ISO3}-summary.csv on every build, and
# nothing reads it: budget work is suspended, so `country.py` does not open it and
# `finance.py` does not aggregate it. Bill removed all 59 from the repo on 2026-08-14
# for that reason; the compiler keeps producing them, so they are ignored rather than
# deleted in a loop. Drop this line when budget work resumes.
outputs/non-state-finance/*-summary.csv

# The index is rebuildable scaffolding and is never committed — the freshness
# sweep in vault_lib is what pays for that. Corpus builds its own (2026-08-14),
# and it belongs in scripts/.workroot/index/, which .workroot/ above already
# covers; an index/ appearing HERE, at the repo root, means a script was run
# with the repo root as ROOT, which indexes a tree holding none of the roots.
# That would be a correct index of nothing, reporting itself *fresh* for ever
# after — so vault_lib now refuses to write it (EmptyIndex) and this line is
# the second line of defence. Committed once on 2026-08-14 (c53dcf7); removed.
index/
